# TMF Intraday Predictive Analytics — Data Sources

## 1. Purpose

This document defines the planned data sources for the TMF Intraday Predictive Analytics project.

The objective is to identify reliable, timestamp-accurate, reproducible data capable of supporting:

1. Historical quantitative research
2. Intraday feature engineering
3. Statistical modeling
4. Walk-forward validation
5. thinkorswim market monitoring
6. paperMoney prospective testing
7. Model-versus-realized performance analysis

A data source will not be incorporated into the modeling pipeline until its historical depth, frequency, timestamp methodology, and leakage risks have been evaluated.

---

# 2. Source Selection Principles

Each candidate data source will be evaluated using:

| Criterion | Requirement |
|---|---|
| Historical depth | Sufficient observations for time-series analysis |
| Intraday frequency | Preferably 1m or 5m for core market variables |
| Timestamp accuracy | Required |
| Timezone documentation | Required |
| Data reliability | High |
| API/download access | Preferred |
| Reproducibility | Required |
| Cost | Documented |
| Rate limits | Documented |
| Licensing | Documented |
| Corporate-action handling | Required for ETFs |
| Revision handling | Required for macroeconomic data |

No source will be selected solely because it is free.

---

# 3. Source Tiers

Data sources will be classified into four tiers.

## Tier 1 — Core Modeling Data

Required for the primary 5-minute predictive model.

Examples:

- TMF
- TLT
- Treasury futures
- Intraday Treasury-market proxies
- SPY
- QQQ

## Tier 2 — Cross-Asset Predictors

Used to test incremental predictive capability.

Examples:

- U.S. dollar
- WTI crude oil
- Gold
- VIX

## Tier 3 — Macro / Regime Data

Used primarily for event and regime modeling.

Examples:

- CPI
- PCE
- GDP
- payrolls
- daily Treasury yields
- Federal Reserve events

## Tier 4 — Validation Platforms

Used for prospective testing rather than historical model estimation.

Primary platform:

- thinkorswim
- paperMoney

